7, 61.217, 61.457, 61.834, 62.119, 62.313, 62.552, 62.699, 62.892, 63.132]}, {"a": 63.39, "b": 65.29, "t": "she may be pulling up a memory.", "k": ["pulling"], "w": [63.44, 63.633, 63.827, 63.974, 64.351, 64.498, 64.6]}, {"a": 65.29, "b": 67.357, "t": "To be fair, it was a small study,", "k": ["study,"], "w": [65.34, 65.521, 65.701, 66.08, 66.261, 66.498, 66.622, 66.972]}, {"a": 67.357, "b": 71.38000000000001, "t": "just 40 dogs, so scientists say more research is needed.", "k": ["40"], "w": [67.407, 67.701, 68.175, 68.554, 68.735, 69.367, 69.604, 69.898, 70.418, 70.599]}, {"a": 71.38000000000001, "b": 74.197, "t": "Try it yourself: say a word your dog knows well,", "k": ["yourself:"], "w": [71.43, 71.658, 71.831, 72.41, 72.638, 72.757, 73.039, 73.32, 73.548, 73.884]}, {"a": 74.197, "b": 76.79, "t": "like ball or walk, and watch the head.", "k": ["walk,"], "w": [74.247, 74.528, 74.81, 74.983, 75.346, 75.574, 75.91, 76.137]}, {"a": 76.79, "b": 79.59, "t": "Signal number two: the direction of the wag.", "k": ["direction"], "w": [76.84, 77.212, 77.584, 77.879, 78.096, 78.623, 78.788, 79.005]}, {"a": 79.59, "b": 82.36, "t": "A wagging tail does not always mean happy.", "k": ["wagging"], "w": [79.64, 79.759, 80.2, 80.481, 80.761, 80.987, 81.375, 81.655]}, {"a": 82.36, "b": 89.13300000000001, "t": "In 2007, Italian scientists found that dogs tend to wag more to the right when they see something they like,", "k": ["2007,"], "w": [82.41, 82.588, 83.408, 83.863, 84.485, 84.829, 85.117, 85.405, 85.694, 85.871, 86.104, 86.393, 86.57, 86.803, 87.147, 87.436, 87.724, 87.957, 88.523, 88.811]}, {"a": 89.13300000000001, "b": 90.71000000000001, "t": "such as their owner.", "k": ["owner."], "w": [89.183, 89.471, 89.649, 89.993]}, {"a": 90.71000000000001, "b": 92.10600000000001, "t": "And more to the left when they", "k": ["more"], "w": [90.76, 90.941, 91.165, 91.303, 91.484, 91.708, 91.932]}, {"a": 92.10600000000001, "b": 94.39, "t": "see something they want to back away from.", "k": ["something"], "w": [92.156, 92.337, 92.777, 93.001, 93.225, 93.363, 93.587, 93.811]}, {"a": 94.39, "b": 95.491, "t": "In 2013,", "k": ["2013,"], "w": [94.44, 94.636]}, {"a": 95.491, "b": 100.12, "t": "the same team showed videos of wagging dogs to 43 other dogs.", "k": ["43"], "w": [95.541, 95.798, 96.116, 96.434, 96.875, 97.315, 97.511, 98.013, 98.331, 98.527, 99.041, 99.42]}, {"a": 100.12, "b": 102.364, "t": "When the dog on screen wagged to the left,", "k": ["screen"], "w": [100.17, 100.428, 100.636, 100.844, 101.002, 101.359, 101.715, 101.874, 102.082]}, {"a": 102.364, "b": 106.29, "t": "the watching dogs' heart rates went up, and they looked more anxious.", "k": ["watching"], "w": [102.414, 102.622, 103.078, 103.335, 103.642, 103.949, 104.207, 104.44, 104.648, 104.905, 105.262, 105.52]}, {"a": 106.29, "b": 108.87, "t": "When it wagged to the right, they stayed relaxed.", "k": ["relaxed."], "w": [106.34, 106.561, 106.696, 107.002, 107.138, 107.316, 107.642, 107.863, 108.168]}, {"a": 108.87, "b": 111.641, "t": "The scientists say it may not be a deliberate message.", "k": ["scientists"], "w": [108.92, 109.122, 109.662, 109.864, 110.019, 110.221, 110.423, 110.578, 110.684, 111.223]}, {"a": 111.641, "b": 115.31, "t": "It could simply come from which side of the brain is more active.", "k": ["active."], "w": [111.691, 111.845, 112.143, 112.49, 112.741, 112.991, 113.29, 113.541, 113.695, 113.897, 114.196, 114.35, 114.601]}, {"a": 115.31, "b": 118.395, "t": "And always read the tail together with the rest of the body,", "k": ["together"], "w": [115.36, 115.563, 115.91, 116.161, 116.364, 116.615, 117.059, 117.31, 117.513, 117.764, 117.919, 118.121]}, {"a": 118.395, "b": 119.57000000000001, "t": "not on its own.", "k": ["own."], "w": [118.445, 118.648, 118.802, 119.005]}, {"a": 119.57000000000001, "b": 121.83, "t": "Signal number three: puppy eyes.", "k": ["Signal"], "w": [119.62, 120.015, 120.41, 120.832, 121.172]}, {"a": 121.83, "b": 124.078, "t": "When your dog raises its inner eyebrows,", "k": ["eyebrows,"], "w": [121.88, 122.152, 122.425, 122.645, 123.022, 123.242, 123.567]}, {"a": 124.078, "b": 126.65, "t": "its eyes look bigger, and a little sad.", "k": ["bigger,"], "w": [124.128, 124.348, 124.62, 124.893, 125.349, 125.569, 125.684, 126.061]}, {"a": 126.65, "b": 127.638, "t": "In 2019,", "k": ["2019,"], "w": [126.7, 126.876]}, {"a": 127.638, "b": 132.20999999999998, "t": "scientists found that dogs have a small muscle that makes this move easy.", "k": ["scientists"], "w": [127.688, 128.303, 128.643, 128.929, 129.214, 129.499, 129.62, 129.96, 130.356, 130.641, 130.981, 131.267, 131.552]}, {"a": 132.20999999999998, "b": 136.36999999999998, "t": "It has a long name: the levator anguli oculi medialis.", "k": ["medialis."], "w": [132.26, 132.471, 132.747, 132.892, 133.235, 133.676, 133.953, 134.493, 134.967, 135.375]}, {"a": 136.36999999999998, "b": 139.31, "t": "Wolves, their wild relatives, barely have it.", "k": ["relatives,"], "w": [136.42, 136.883, 137.212, 137.489, 138.111, 138.494, 138.77]}, {"a": 139.31, "b": 143.6, "t": "Dogs also make this face more often, and more intensely, than wolves.", "k": ["intensely,"], "w": [139.36, 139.638, 139.916, 140.194, 140.472, 140.75, 141.028, 141.439, 141.664, 141.942, 142.567, 142.845]}, {"a": 143.6, "b": 145.96599999999998, "t": "An earlier study found that shelter dogs", "k": ["earlier"], "w": [143.65, 143.829, 144.286, 144.632, 144.978, 145.268, 145.726]}, {"a": 145.96599999999998, "b": 149.38, "t": "that raised their eyebrows more were adopted faster.", "k": ["eyebrows"], "w": [146.016, 146.306, 146.708, 147.053, 147.567, 147.857, 148.147, 148.605]}, {"a": 149.38, "b": 152.15599999999998, "t": "Scientists think that, over thousands of years,", "k": ["years,"], "w": [149.43, 150.047, 150.389, 150.758, 151.044, 151.606, 151.782]}, {"a": 152.15599999999998, "b": 156.64999999999998, "t": "humans may have favored dogs with this look, without even realizing it.", "k": ["realizing"], 